  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Management of the Bay of Bengal Large Marine Ecosystem (BOBLME) - FULL SIZE PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The  b project development objective (PDO) /B  is to support the development of a Strategic Action Programme (SAP) whose implementation will lead to enhanced food security and reduced poverty for coastal communities in the BOB region, consistent and linked with a sustained resource base of good ecosystem quality. br  B 
(i)  /b identifying sound policies leading to strengthening
community-based approaches to integrated coastal resources management,  br  B (ii)  /b empowering local communities to participate in processes and decisions associated with the development of sub-regional and regional fishery management plans, and  br  B (iii) /b  increasing options such as access to alternative livelihood opportunities. The &quot;lessons&quot; derived from these activities will be fed into SAP design. br 
The project has been structured into five interlinking components. br 
 B Component 1: /B  Strategic Action Programme br 
 B Component 2:  /B  Coastal/Marine Natural Resources Management and Sustainable Use br 
 B Component 3:  /B  Improved Understanding and Predictability of the BOBLME Environment  br 
 b Component 4: /B  Maintenance of Ecosystem Health and Management of Pollution  br 
 B Component 5: /B  Project Management, Monitoring and Evaluation and Knowledge Management</narrative>
  </description>
